  "notes": "\"Deftly played bass lines\" is the research's own phrase and it is the whole model: continuous syncopated funk with slides, dead notes and octave pops, the loudest melodic element in the Bay mix. That is the most free bass on this axis — `followRootsProb` 0.25, `glideProb` 0.72, `anticipationProb` 0.5, `P8` in the passing tones for the octave pops, and four cell shapes that all start from a chord tone because the research says his vocabulary is chord-tone-plus-blue-note. He is also credited on drums, which is why this entry has a *lower* quantize strength than any other in the batch: live overdubs on top of a sampled kit, human fills at section boundaries. The second guitar chair makes the countermelody the busiest here at 0.7 — his parts run continuously, so the arrangement contrast is layers entering and leaving over a constant rhythm section, hence a low `dropOutBeats.prob` against a raised `switchUpProb`. ⚠ Register is the research's E1–G2 with headroom at the top so the bass generator has a reachable pool; the floor is unchanged. ⚠ `modes` are authored because the parent's Death Row moods pin 90–100 and his band is 84–96. ⚠ `medium` per the research's medium-high; the playing is documented, the tempo band is catalog-level.",
